# Settings for the gbs-anywhere service (installed as
# /etc/default/gbs-anywhere). After a change:
#   sudo systemctl restart gbs-anywhere
#
# Most settings are easier in the app. Environment variables as in the
# README, for example an E65/E80 GbS grinder's address:
#GRINDER_HOST=192.168.1.30
#UPDATE_CHECK=off
#
# Extra flags (see `gbs-anywhere --help`), for example another port when
# port 80 is taken (fine for an E65/E80; the E64 WS needs port 80):
#GBS_ANYWHERE_ARGS=-p 8080
